  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a3d2b5e5b8bd75781820de5be38f0970, type: 3}
  m_Name: ExhibitData_computer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ExhibitData
  exhibitName: THE COMPUTER
  pages:
  - "The first computers were SO big they filled an entire room!\nThey weighed as
    much as 10 elephants and could only\ndo simple math. There were no screens, no
    mouse,\nand definitely no games just thousands of wires\nand blinking lights.\n
    \nThe people who operated them were mostly women,\nknown as \"human computers\"
    because their job\nwas to calculate numbers by hand before the machines took
    over."
  - "The first computer mouse was made of wood!\nIt was invented in 1964 and had
    just one button.\n \nToday, the phone in your pocket is MILLIONS of times\nmore
    powerful than those giant room-sized machines.\nFrom a metal box as big as a
    house to something\nthat fits in your hand that's the magic of invention! \U0001F4BB"
  exhibitIllustration: {fileID: 1152356169552002576, guid: 69f06ed49f9286d029c418756af7526f, type: 3}
  narratorClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f18f05dfc5384a062ad29dbae3446302, type: 3}
